{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-2786","published":"2026-06-24T11:11:42Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:21:12.161196391Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-42250"],"summary":"bzip2 security update","details":"bzip2 is a freely available, patent free, high-quality data compressor. It typically compresses files to within 10% to 15% of the best available techniques (the PPM family of statistical compressors), whilst being around twice as fast at compression and six times faster at decompression.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nbzip2 contains an off‑by‑one error in the bzip2recover utility. When processing a specially crafted file, the application performs an out‑of‑bounds write to a global buffer, resulting in memory corruption and a crash (denial of service).\n\nThis issue was fixed in bzip2 patch 35d122a3df8b0cc4082a4d89fdc6ee99f375fe67(CVE-2026-42250)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"bzip2","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP1","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/bzip2&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.0.8-9.oe2403sp1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["bzip2-1.0.8-9.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","bzip2-debuginfo-1.0.8-9.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","bzip2-debugsource-1.0.8-9.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","bzip2-devel-1.0.8-9.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["bzip2-help-1.0.8-9.oe2403sp1.noarch.rpm"],"src":["bzip2-1.0.8-9.oe2403sp1.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["bzip2-1.0.8-9.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","bzip2-debuginfo-1.0.8-9.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","bzip2-debugsource-1.0.8-9.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","bzip2-devel-1.0.8-9.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-2786.json"}},{"package":{"name":"bzip2","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/bzip2&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.0.8-9.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["bzip2-1.0.8-9.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","bzip2-debuginfo-1.0.8-